This implementation uses the Polars Rust crate (a modern, high-performance DataFrame library). It builds a DataFrame from the input, checks that each column has at least one non-missing value (otherwise returns an error, since a column mean cannot be computed), fills nulls with the column mean, and returns the filled data in row-major order.

